---
title: Vegan Pad Thai (Pad Mee Korat)
portions: 2
category: Thai
source: "https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/vegan-pad-thai/"
---

## Prep ~{-1h}

[Soak] Soak the @rice-noodles{112 g} in room-temperature water for ~{1 h}, then drain.

[Mix] In a #small bowl{}, mash the @soybean-paste{25 g} with a fork, then stir in the @soy-sauce{15 ml}, the @tamarind-paste{40 g}, the @chili-flakes{2 g} and the @water{45 ml}. ->&pad thai sauce{}

## Stir-fry

[Sear] Heat @vegetable-oil{15 ml} in a #wok{} over medium-high heat. Sear the @pressed-tofu{85 g} and the @shiitake{100 g} until golden, ~{3 min}. Remove from the pan.

[Caramelize] Add the remaining @vegetable-oil{30 ml} with the @garlic{4} and the @shallot{40 g} and the @palm-sugar{35 g}. Cook, stirring, until deep brown, ~{2 min}.

[Deglaze] Pour in the &pad thai sauce{}.

[Toss] Add the soaked @rice-noodles{112 g} with the seared tofu and mushrooms. Toss until all the sauce is absorbed, ~{3 min}.

[Finish] Off the heat, toss in the @bean-sprouts{50 g} and the @garlic-chives{40 g}. Plate and sprinkle with the @roasted-peanuts{25 g}.
